WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.501
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.003
Thank you so much for watching.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.239
My name is Jimmy Fallon.
That is The Roots right there.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:09.475
And welcome to our show. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.144
It's interesting.
You guys got a...

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:12.444
-Aw.
-...lot more --

00:00:12.444 --> 00:00:14.814
[ Laughter ]
Lot more applause.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.316
That's alright.
We'll fix it in post, right?

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.684
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.552
[ Recorded cheers and applause
plays, stops abruptly ]

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.355
Well --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.389
Let's get to some news.

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.524
Guys, a lot of people
are talking

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.259
about President Trump's
press conference

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:28.127
in the Rose Garden yesterday.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:29.595
Things went pretty
off the rails.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.630
If you didn't see it,
here are some highlights.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.599
I'll let you be the judge.

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:36.236
-If we did half the testing,
we'd have half the cases.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:40.206
If we did another --
You cut that in half,

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.275
we'd have yet again
half of that.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:47.480
So, Joe Bi-- Joe Biden
wants to end school choice,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.883
abolish educational standards,

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:53.519
abolish in the suburbs --

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.454
You're going to abolish
the suburbs with this.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.189
Tens of thousands of bridges...
-[ Laughing ] What?!

00:00:57.189 --> 00:01:00.493
-...are in disrepair
and on the verge of collapse.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.395
Well, it's probably
not a right number,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.931
but we have bridges
that should have been fixed.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.932
-Yeah. [ As Trump ]
"Ten -- Tens of thousands --

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.601
Look, it's probably not
a right number.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.102
Why would I even say a number?

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.171
150 million bridges."

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.674
[ Normal voice ]
Usually when you see
something like that on TV,

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:17.210
it ends with a voice saying,
"It's time to ask your doctor

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.712
if Abilify is right for you."

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.180
Seriously, if that were
a wedding toast,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.516
the groom would have wrestled
the mic away after 10 seconds,

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.417
like, "What are you
talking about?

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:27.253
Sit down!"

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.521
The sun was listening like,

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:29.855
"Hey, don't blame the heat.
This is all him.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:31.857
I had nothing to do with this."

00:01:31.857 --> 00:01:34.961
Normally, when a 74-year-old man
spends an hour yelling

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.695
in his garden,
his family's like,

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:39.799
"Time to go look
at some homes for Grandpa."

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.767
Look, I'll just say it --
Trump hasn't been the same

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.369
since he stopped drink bleach.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.205
Alright? I'm --

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.774
[ Babbles indistinctly ]

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.376
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.710
And instead of
a press conference,

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.712
people said it was more like
a campaign rally

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:55.681
in front of 20 people.

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:57.550
In other words,
it was just like Tulsa.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.451
-Ooh.
-Ooh.

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:00.753
-Oh.
-Too soon.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.122
-Oh. Too soon. I stung.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.391
I float like a butterfly
but sting still.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.294
Still -- I still sting --
sting a little bit.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.996
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.996 --> 00:02:13.432
That's the famous slogan.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:14.501
Fly like a butterfly,

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.936
but I still sting
a little bit, though.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.070
Be careful.
-Little bit.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.805
-Just be careful.

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:21.507
Meanwhile, the Biden
campaign responded

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.076
and called the press conference
a sad affair.

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:26.011
Trump defended himself,
yelling, "Fake news.

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:28.681
All my affairs have been happy.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.149
[ Crew groans ]

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:31.584
Well, most of them.
Most of them."

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.552
I don't know if you guys
have been following this,

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:36.388
but there has been a call
to boycott Goya Foods

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:38.824
after their CEO praised Trump
last week.

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.594
So last night, Ivanka Trump
decided to show her support

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:45.465
for the company. And, well,
just take a look at this.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:48.501
Yeah. Sadly, after Ivanka
tweeted in Spanish,

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.369
Trump immediately
had her deported.

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.071
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.107
-I'm not sure if Ivanka
is trying to promote Goya

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.876
or she's auditioning to be a
model on "The Price is Right."

00:02:56.876 --> 00:03:00.146
♪♪

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:06.218
"A new car-r-r-r!

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:09.288
A new jet ski!"

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.590
"Uh, I live in Kansas."

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.226
"You're still going to want
that jet ski."

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.960
Trump saw that and was like,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.330
"Why is Ivanka holding
Don Jr.'s inheritance?"

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.198
-Ah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.934
-But it didn't stop there 'cause
after Ivanka's tweet went viral,

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:25.171
Trump tweeted this morning to
also show his support for Goya.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.340
He wrote,
"@GoyaFoods is doing GREAT.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.775
The Radical Left
smear machine backfired,

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:32.311
people are buying like crazy!"

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:35.248
Americans are like, "We're
buying canned food like crazy

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.250
'cause we're living
in the apocalypse!

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.885
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.320
Hello?"

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.088
But Trump wasn't done yet,
'cause this afternoon,

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:44.891
he posted this photo
on Instagram.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:45.958
Take a look.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.126
-Oh.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.895
-Yeah. Even weirder,
the caption was,

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:52.065
"Great meeting with my cabinet."
What does that mean?

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.367
What the hell is happening --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.368
We have a raging pandemic
on our hands,

00:03:56.368 --> 00:03:59.638
and he's practicing
for "Supermarket Sweep."

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:01.440
I think those are Trump's
four major food groups --

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.443
bags, bottles, cans, and boxes.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.810
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.578
Well, at least,
that's one Mexican wall

00:04:06.578 --> 00:04:08.014
Trump's managed to build.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.182
[ Crew laughs, groans ]

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:11.251
Is he the president

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.486
or a divorced dad
checking out at a Publix?

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.786
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.786 --> 00:04:16.188
"Couple cans of beans,

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:19.558
and...I'll have some
chocolate cookies.

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:22.661
Sheila's not coming back."
[ Clears throat ]

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:24.697
Guys, as health officials
are trying to find out

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.499
as much as they can
about the virus,

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.334
the White House
announced a new way

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.469
pandemic data should be handled.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.571
I'm not sure this is the answer.
Listen to this.

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:35.541 line:0%
-The Trump administration
is ordering hospitals

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.810 line:0%
to send patient data
to Washington, D.C.,

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:42.382 line:0%
before the actual CDC.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.682
-So remember that next week

00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:46.218
when Trump announces
that there are zero new cases.

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:48.321
"You're welcome.
There's no more cases.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.855
Here's the data right here.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.557
Where is my hurricane Sharpie?

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:55.160
There you go. Cross that out.
Zero cases.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.929
I did good. Now bean me."

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.399
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:02.068
Some businesses are also
taking their own measures

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.836
to help stop the spread
of the virus.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.272
-Walmart will start
requiring masks

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:10.542
for shoppers at all of
its stores starting next Monday.

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.579
-Yep, Walmart will require
customers to wear masks,

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.281
but they're still
pants-optional.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:17.984
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:19.552
Also if you try to walk in
without a mask,

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:23.089
prepare to be clotheslined
by a 85-year-old greeter.

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.224
"Oh, here comes the thunder.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.060
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.564
[ Whack! ]

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:34.267
You broke my arm."

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.735
[ Chuckles ]

00:05:35.735 --> 00:05:38.638
A spokesman for Walmart was
like, "Listen, this is Walmart.

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:40.907
You should have been wearing
a face mask this entire time.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.274
Come on."

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:44.543
And the virus isn't only
affecting the retail industry.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:45.744
The entertainment world

00:05:45.744 --> 00:05:47.513
is also having to make
some tough decisions.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:50.850 line:0%
-"Survivor" will not return
with a new season this fall.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.185 line:0%
The show was supposed
to shoot in March

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:55.654 line:0%
but stopped
because of the pandemic.

00:05:55.654 --> 00:05:57.790
-Ah, that's my favorite show,
man. That's a bummer.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.058
But honestly, it's fine

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.827
considering we're all
pretty much living through

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:03.362
one giant episode of "Survivor."

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.931
So for everyone keeping track,
the pandemic is too dangerous

00:06:05.931 --> 00:06:08.401
for the Mogi Pucha tribe
to stay on their island,

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:11.403
but it's fine for kids K through
12 to go back to school.

00:06:11.403 --> 00:06:12.471
-Oh.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.773
-Aw.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:17.009
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:18.177
-What you talking about, man?

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:21.814
-Too soon.
-Yeah.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.816
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:31.023 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:33.859
I got to do, like, a physical
bit if the joke tanks.

00:06:33.859 --> 00:06:34.961
-Yeah, no. I loved that, man.

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.161
-You like that?
That's pretty good?

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:39.131
-Yo, you should do
a physical bit always.

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:47.440
-"Where are you?"

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.542
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.011
And finally, guys, I heard

00:06:53.011 --> 00:06:56.449
that Hallmark just launched
a line of Christmas-themed wines

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:58.684
that are available
for pre-order now.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.219
Huh. Seems a bit early to me.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:03.289
But I don't know. Check out
this ad Hallmark released.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:07.059
-We here at Hallmark know you've
been cooped up for a while now.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.828
And that's why
we're already thinking

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:11.497
about bringing you some joy
this holiday.

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:14.332
Hallmark's Christmas wine
is available for pre-order,

00:07:14.332 --> 00:07:15.600
so get your bottle t--

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.969
-Sold out.
-Oh.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:19.472
[ Chuckles ] Uh, well, that --
that went fast.

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.806
But don't worry.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:24.443
We're also launching our
brand-new Valentine's Day wine,

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:25.611
available for pre-order --

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.913
-Sold out.
-Wow. Really?

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:30.983
Well, good thing there are
plenty of holidays to celebrate,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:33.552
with our St. Patrick's Day wine.
-Sold out.

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:35.888
-Our Arbor Day wine.
-Sold out.

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:37.690
-Our New Year's Eve 2026 wine.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.458
-Sold out.
-Nope. Good God.

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:41.260
Okay. I think I need a drink.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.595
-Sold out.
-Of course it is.

00:07:43.595 --> 00:07:46.899 line:0%
Hallmark Wines. Just put
your name on the waitlist.

